  "body_html": "<h1>Ordered-Bid Utilities</h1>\n<p>For finite linearly ordered bid spaces, the auction library provides maximum\nbid, argmax bidder, and maximum-bid-excluding-one-bidder utilities.</p>\n<p>These utilities support concrete auction rules such as first-price and\nsecond-price auctions.</p>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[MFoGT, Chapter 1, Section 1.2.4 and Exercise 4] Maschler, Solan, and\n  Zamir, <em>Game Theory</em>, <code>references/GameTheory.pdf</code>. Highest-bid and\n  second-highest-bid comparisons in the Vickrey auction example.</li>\n<li>[AGT, Chapter 1, Section 1.3.2] Nisan, Roughgarden, Tardos, and Vazirani,\n  <em>Algorithmic Game Theory</em>, <code>references/AlgorithmicGameTheory.pdf</code>.\n  Second-price auction payoffs and ordered bid comparisons.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Provenance</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Migrated from EconCSLib pull request 27, old blueprint label\n  <code>def:auction_basic_ordered_bids</code> in <code>blueprint/src/content.tex</code>.</li>\n</ul>",
  "proof_html": null,
